From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:55:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ims: give the compat ImsService adapters a default executor

Binding any compat ImsService (android.telephony.ims.compat.ImsService --
the path a bridge to an OEM's pre-P com.android.ims stack has to use) kills
com.android.phone immediately and it restart-loops:

  FATAL EXCEPTION: ImsProvisioningController
  java.lang.NullPointerException
    at java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture.screenExecutor
    at ImsConfigImplBase$ImsConfigStub.executeMethodAsync
    at ImsConfigImplBase$ImsConfigStub.addImsConfigCallback
    at com.android.ims.ImsConfig.addConfigCallback
    at ImsProvisioningController$MmTelFeatureListener.connectionReady

Every *ImplBase dispatches its binder calls through
CompletableFuture.runAsync(.., mExecutor), and ImsConfigImplBase's no-arg
constructor leaves that executor null. The modern path never hits it because
ImsService#getConfig/getRegistration/createMmTelFeature each call
setDefaultExecutor() on the stub they return; createMMTelCompat() creates the
three compat adapters and calls it on none of them. A null executor there is
not a fall back to the calling thread -- screenExecutor() throws -- so the
first framework call into the adapter is fatal.

Set it on all three (MmTel feature, registration and config adapters): the
other two reach the same runAsync and would fail the same way on the next
call. Found bringing LG's Ims4 up on 24.0; the compat path has been
deprecated since P and nothing in tree exercises it.

---
 .../telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java  | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java
index 6b9866968c..9ef4a4ffb6 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ims/ImsServiceControllerCompat.java
@@ -264,8 +264,18 @@ public class ImsServiceControllerCompat extends ImsServiceController {
         ImsRegistrationCompatAdapter regAdapter = new ImsRegistrationCompatAdapter();
         mmTelAdapter.addRegistrationAdapter(regAdapter);
         mRegCompatAdapters.put(slotId, regAdapter);
-        mConfigCompatAdapters.put(slotId, new ImsConfigCompatAdapter(
-                mmTelAdapter.getOldConfigInterface()));
+        ImsConfigCompatAdapter configAdapter = new ImsConfigCompatAdapter(
+                mmTelAdapter.getOldConfigInterface());
+        mConfigCompatAdapters.put(slotId, configAdapter);
+        // The modern path does this in ImsService#getConfig/getRegistration/createMmTelFeature;
+        // nothing does it for the compat adapters, and every *ImplBase routes its binder calls
+        // through CompletableFuture.runAsync(..., mExecutor). A null executor there is not a
+        // fallback to the calling thread -- screenExecutor() throws NPE -- so the first framework
+        // call (ImsProvisioningController -> ImsConfig#addConfigCallback) kills com.android.phone
+        // and it restart-loops as soon as a compat ImsService is bound.
+        mmTelAdapter.setDefaultExecutor(mExecutor);
+        regAdapter.setDefaultExecutor(mExecutor);
+        configAdapter.setDefaultExecutor(mExecutor);
         return mmTelAdapter.getBinder();
     }
 
